1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
03:17 runs approved maintenance while operators sleep.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Gemini plans and replans. Deterministic Evidence Gates authorize every action.

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:30,000
One approved request starts the workflow through Pub/Sub and Cloud Run.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:44,000
The agent discovers topology, health, capacity, runbooks, and rollback requirements.

5
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:58,000
WEB01 drains, updates to v1.1.0, passes verification, and rejoins the load balancer.

6
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:12,000
WEB02 updates, but its functional test fails even though readiness passed.

7
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:26,000
The agent collects logs and metrics, then Gemini replans from the observed failure.

8
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:41,000
The rollback gate verifies ownership of the recovery point before restoration.

9
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:53,000
WEB02 returns to v1.0.0, becomes healthy, and rollback verification passes.

10
00:01:53,000 --> 00:02:04,000
The database gate blocks the next change because target-version redundancy is false.

11
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Final outcome: WEB01 updated; WEB02 rolled back; database safely deferred.

12
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:17,200
Availability preserved. Human interventions: zero.

13
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:21,200
Cloud Run serves the deployed application in europe-west1.

14
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:25,200
Firestore persists structured maintenance evidence and audit events.

15
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:29,200
Pub/Sub delivers the approved request to the maintenance worker.

16
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:33,200
Cloud Logging proves Gemini 3.5 Flash requests through Vertex AI.

17
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:37,200
Correlated logs retain the maintenance ID and tool outcomes.
